    GPL-3.0 License | Contributors: see git history

    PlayerView with TextureView surface_type. Used below API 34
    (UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE) where SurfaceView's surface re-creation would
    require re-creating the video codec on every fullscreen toggle /
    orientation change. TextureView can move between parent surfaces
    without re-creating the codec, at the cost of the well-known
    stale-frame issue (mitigated by VideoSurfaceManager's PlaceholderSurface
    keeping the codec alive + the existing kickRenderer() micro-cycle).

    Ported from Flow's app/src/main/res/layout/video_player_view.xml.
-->
<androidx.media3.ui.PlayerView
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/video_artwork_player_view"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="#000000"
    app:use_controller="false"
    app:surface_type="texture_view"
    app:keep_content_on_player_reset="false" />
